      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm stuck on an iam issue. i'm trying to let a lambda function write logs to an s3 bucket but im just getting \"access denied\" errors even though i thought i added the policy right. can u check this json for me?\n\n{\n  \"Version\": \"2012-10-17\",\n  \"Statement\": [\n    {\n      \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n      \"Action\": [\n        \"s3:PutObject\"\n      ],\n      \"Resource\": \"arn:aws:s3:::my-company-logs/*\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That policy should typically grant the necessary permissions to put an object into your S3 bucket. The issue might be related to IAM roles and trust policies. First, make sure that the role assumed by your Lambda function has a trust relationship policy allowing it to assume the role. Check if the IAM policy is associated with the correct role. If you have multiple roles to consider, you may also need to narrow down the permissions using \"Condition: StringEquals\" to limit them to just the Lambda function's required actions.",
